+# The Daily Grind
+
+Coffee shop homepage with a customer **My Account** area (`/account`) supporting passkeys.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start            # builds the WebAuthn polyfill bundle, then starts the server on :11222
+```
+
+| Env var    | Default                     | Purpose                                                        |
+| ---------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `PORT`     | `11222`                     | Listen port                                                    |
+| `ORIGIN`   | `http://localhost:$PORT`    | Exact public origin (WebAuthn verifies this; must be HTTPS in production) |
+| `RP_ID`    | hostname of `ORIGIN`        | WebAuthn Relying Party ID (e.g. `dailygrind.example` to cover subdomains) |
+| `DATA_DIR` | `./data`                    | JSON store for accounts/passkeys and the cached AAGUID registry |
+
+## Account features
+
+- **Registration** – email, name and password; afterwards customers are offered a passkey (platform authenticator).
+- **Sign-in** – email/password with passkey autofill (conditional mediation) plus a "Sign in with a passkey" button.
+  After a password sign-in, a passkey is silently offered via conditional create where supported.
+- **Passkey management** – list (provider name/icon from the AAGUID registry, created/last-used dates),
+  create (security keys allowed), rename, delete. The list is synced to password managers with
+  `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials()`.
+- **Profile updates** – name and email; synced with `signalCurrentUserDetails()`.
+- **Reauthentication** – creating/deleting passkeys and profile changes require identity confirmation within
+  the last 5 minutes, using one of the customer's own passkeys (`allowCredentials`, UV required) or their password.
+
+Server: `server/index.js` (Node `http` + `@simplewebauthn/server`). Client: `public/js/webauthn.js`, `public/js/account.js`.
+Sessions are in memory and data is a JSON file. Use a real session store and database in production.
